  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "1. Ether-Mach Firmware",
    "description": "Developed high-frequency real-time motion control firmware in C/VHDL for Stepper3's Ether-Mach motion control system. \n\nThe tight real-time control of this firmware gave the Ether-Mach system a competitive edge via smooth, precise motion. The better-than-expected performance allowed Stepper3 to sell to higher end markets than were originally expected. \n\nAdditionally, by recognizing the need for and creating flexible and extensible firmware, Stepper3 was not only able to release its own flagship CNC control system, but also able to release multiple customized systems for individual clients with few modifications to the firmware. The flexibility of this firmware widened Stepper3’s customer base and brought in new opportunities using only a single base design with minimal re-engineering.\n",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": ""
   },
   {
    "title": "2. FTUI",
    "description": "Developed an OpenGL style API to create graphics and GUIs with the FTDI FT800 graphics controller. Built for Stepper3 LLC and released under the GNU GPLv3, this library allows for fast iterative GUI development for small microcontrollers. This helped Stepper3 meet quick deadlines on a contract to modernize a client’s product line using touchscreen interfaces.\n\nUnlike traditional UI frameworks, which rely on a retained widget hierarchy, FTUI implements an immediate mode GUI, or IMGUI, API. This API style, originally popularized in the game industry for making quick debug interfaces, is ideal for UI construction on RAM constrained microcontrollers since it does not rely on storing large amounts of widget data. For more details, see the project link below to the Github README.\n",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": ""
   }
